  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through next Friday)\nIssued at 356 PM EDT Sat Oct 10 2026\n\nAs the remnants of Isaias pull to the north and east, an area of \ndrier air will emerge from the central United States and move into \nthe region by Tuesday. While high temperatures may not see a drastic \nchange behind this frontal boundary, dewpoint values and low \ntemperatures could offer some relief from the tropically support \nwarmth we have experienced over the last few days.\n\nLarger-scale high pressure will build at the surface over a good \nportion of the southeastern United States by mid-week which will \nhelp the drier air linger over the region until late in the week. \nEventually the high will shift slightly north and open the door for \nthe return of moist easterly flow from the Caribbean and Atlantic \nover South Florida. With that shift in pattern also comes a return \nfor shower and thunderstorm chances across South Florida to close \nout the forecast period.",
